issue_context.body:
Repro:
```C#
[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(PublicMethods)]
class AnnotatedBase
{
}

void Test(IEnumerable<AnnotatedBase> instances)
{
  foreach (AnnotatedBase instance in instances)
  {
    instance.GetType().GetMethod("Test"); // Warns: IL2075
  }
}
```

The problem is that the `instance` value is evaluated as a return value from `IEnumerator<AnnotatedBase>.get_Current()`. Linker will not correctly resolve that type (which is declared as a generic parameter) and will end up analyzing `instance` as not having a known static type.

This is a general problem with ability to resolve type of a generic parameter given a proper instantiation.
